From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+alilinux@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:53:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mips: ali-c3503d: built-in initramfs from the SDK
 rootfs tree

The initramfs list carries only the console node (needed before devtmpfs);
the tree itself is the rootfs/ link, which the SDK points at its out/rootfs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/mips/ali-c3503d/initramfs.list | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/mips/ali-c3503d/initramfs.list

diff --git a/arch/mips/ali-c3503d/initramfs.list b/arch/mips/ali-c3503d/initramfs.list
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..193c4b40
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/mips/ali-c3503d/initramfs.list
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+# Built-in initramfs for the ALi C3503D (gen_init_cpio list; paths relative to the kernel build root).
+# The tree itself comes from arch/mips/ali-c3503d/rootfs/: a link to the SDK's out/rootfs (assembled
+# by scripts/20-userspace.sh from rootfs/skeleton and the built programs; not in the kernel tree).
+# Only what a plain directory cannot carry lives here: the console node, needed before devtmpfs.
+dir /dev 0755 0 0
+nod /dev/console 0600 0 0 c 5 1
